<div id="2026-09-10-receipt-vs-bill-ask-before-write" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-09-10 — Receipt vs bill: ask before writing</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> The AI now detects when pasted text is a card RECEIPT (money already paid) rather than an unpaid bill, and asks which kind to record instead of guessing.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> <code>inventory_supplier_invoices</code> is an AP BILL — it has <code>due_date</code>, <code>ap_account_id</code>, and a <code>draft → posted → paid</code> lifecycle, and NO payment/paid columns. A receipt for money already paid (e.g. "Paid / Amount paid / Visa -3627 / Receipt #", often for prepaid credits) is the opposite: it is settled, not owed. Saving it as <code>status='draft'</code> asserted we still owed the money.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>How.</strong> <code>detect_create_intent</code> now returns <code>looks_paid</code>, <code>looks_prepaid</code>, and <code>payment_card</code> (card + last-4). <code>create_from_params</code> checks these BEFORE the DB handle is needed (asking must not depend on the DB) and returns <code>need_kind</code> with three options: <strong>bill</strong> (draft AP, we owe), <strong>paid</strong> (settled AP, status=paid, card noted), <strong>prepaid</strong> (credits paid up front). The user passes <code>record_kind</code> to answer; only then does it write.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Verified.</strong> Your OpenRouter receipt → looks_paid YES, prepaid YES, card "Visa -3627", USD. A real unpaid bill → looks_paid no. "Paid by cheque" → looks_paid YES. The guard fires with no DB present; with <code>record_kind=paid</code> it proceeds past the guard.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>Comserv/lib/Comserv/Model/AI2/InvoiceCreate.pm</code>.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Not done.</strong> "prepaid" is offered as an option but not yet implemented — <code>inventory_suppliers.prepaid_accno_id</code> exists and models a vendor prepaid balance, but nothing populates or draws it down. Wiring that is a separate change.</p>
</div>
